      "id": "hackernews-2026-05-26-sage-care-yc-s24-is-hiring-software-engineers",
      "title": "Sage Care (YC S24) Is Hiring Software Engineers",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/sagecare/jobs/xtloH8r-senior-software-engineer\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48282478\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Automating home care agency operations with AIFounding Software Engineer$125K - $250K•0.02% - 2.00%•New York, NY, US / Miami, FL, USRoleEngineering, Full stackConnect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About the roleAbout Sage Care\nHome care agencies run on relationships — but they're drowning in paperwork. Intake coordinators spend hours manually transcribing calls, building care plans, and chasing follow-ups. That overhead slows agencies down and pulls their attention away from the people they're trying to serve.\nSage is building the operating system for home care agencies — an AI-native CRM and virtual assistant that turns every client call and home visit into structured care plans, follow-up tasks, and system records, automatically.\nWe integrate directly with the tools agencies already use (WellSky, AxisCare), work on iOS and desktop, and save agencies over 100 minutes per client intake.\nWe're early, well-funded, and signing agencies fast. Now we're looking for the engineers who'll help us build what comes next.\nAs one of Sage’s earliest engineering hires, you’ll play a crucial role in shaping our technical foundation and driving the development of our platform. Reporting directly to the CTO, you’ll have a significant impact on the company's trajectory and growth.\nYou will be responsible for:\nImplementing agents tailored to the home care industry\nDesigning, developing, and maintaining our Django application and native iOS app\nImplementing responsive and interactive front-end features using Datastar\nCreating beautiful and accessible user interfaces with Tailwind CSS and SwiftUI\nCollaborating with the founders to define product roadmap and features\nTranslating business requirements into technical specifications\nConducting code reviews and maintaining high code quality standards\nEvaluating and implementing new technologies to improve our stack, such as what technologies we should choose for our mobile apps\nEstablishing best practices for software development and documentation\nPlanning for future technical needs as the company grows\nComfortable defining your own scope and operating with autonomy\n4+ years of professional experience in full-stack web development\nProficiency with Python and/or iOS development\nKnowledge of Tailwind CSS and component libraries like DaisyUI, Basecoat\nExperience working in a HIPAA environment\nExperience in early-stage startups or as a founding engineer\nA chance to take end to end ownership over what you build\nChoice of location in New York or Miami\nOpportunity to shape the technical direction of a growing startup\nAbout Sage CareHome care agencies run on relationships — but they're drowning in paperwork. Intake coordinators spend hours manually transcribing calls, building care plans, and chasing follow-ups. That overhead slows agencies down and pulls their attention away from the people they're trying to serve.\nSage is building the operating system for home care agencies — an AI-native CRM and virtual assistant that turns every client call and home visit into structured care plans, follow-up tasks, and system records, automatically.\nWe integrate directly with the tools agencies already use (WellSky, AxisCare), work on iOS and desktop, and save agencies over 100 minutes per client intake.\nWe're early, well-funded, and signing agencies fast. Now we're looking for the engineers who'll help us build what comes next.",
