      "body": "Getty ImagesPerfect weather for an ice cream in Bournemouth  The UK has recorded its hottest-ever May temperature as the mercury rose to 34.8C in Kew Gardens in south-west London. Many other areas in the south-east of England also reached temperatures in the 30s.BBC Weather said highs expected in parts of the UK on Monday and Tuesday could exceed top temperatures in Lagos, Cairo and Ho Chi Minh City. The Met Office said the heat would be \"exceptional in the UK even in mid-summer, let alone in May\".An amber health alert issued by the UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA) also remains in place warning that there is a risk of a significant impact across health and social care services.PA MediaCooling down on Bournemouth's beachesPA MediaThe NHS warned people to keep hydrated, with babies, children and older adults at the highest risk of dehydrationIn Pictures via Getty ImagesA picture-perfect view of Greenwich park in south-east LondonBBC Weather Watchers/ Lucie JohnsonPunts on the River Cherwell in OxfordBBC Weather Watchers/ Walking TractorA field red with poppies in Salthouse, NorfolkBBC Weather Watchers/ Linda's LocalCows seeking shade under a tree in a field in Crook of Devon, Perth and KinrossBBC Weather Watchers/ Pauls CameraTaking a rest at the Trentham Monkey Forest in Tittensor, Stoke-on-TrentBBC Weather Watchers/ Lord TenbyIn Wales, people flocked to Tenby North Beach in PembrokeshireGetty ImagesA birdseye view of beachgoers in Falmouth, Cornwall Getty ImagesA boy makes his selection at a beach stall in Southend Getty ImagesConvertible car weather in Rosedale Abbey, North Yorkshire MoorsBBC Weather Watchers/ Danny McGuiganThis feathered family was on the move in the sunshineGetty ImagesTwo families enjoying the views in Rosedale Abbey, North YorkshireBBC Weather Watchers/ SilverloonCharity Age UK recommended staying inside during the hottest hours of the day",
